{"data":{"id":"FenjWjQ8llQ","slug":"jimmy-edgar","title":"Jimmy Edgar","artwork":null,"tracks":[{"id":"oVjFBSFtfBk","slug":"lblb-detroit","title":"LBLB Detroit"},{"id":"YymD5zLOo8M","slug":"sleep-connexion","title":"Sleep Connexion"},{"id":"YZdtHW_DNWM","slug":"hydrant","title":"Hydrant"},{"id":"3xyVu4l6Fk8","slug":"feel-what-it-is","title":"Feel What It Is"}]},"markers":[{"id":"l1Xm05Z0kmA","position":40,"timestamp":"01:33:09","rawTrack":"Jimmy Edgar - LBLB Detroit","track":{"id":"oVjFBSFtfBk","path":"/artists/jimmy-edgar/tracks/lblb-detroit/","slug":"lblb-detroit","title":"LBLB Detroit","artist":{"slug":"jimmy-edgar","title":"Jimmy Edgar"},"artwork":"images/artists/jimmy-edgar/tracks/lblb-detroit.jpg"},"chapter":{"show":{"id":"9MtqvaStm34","slug":"547","tags":[6,3,6,15],"links":{"appleMusic":"https://music.apple.com/gb/station/episode-547/ra.1619426080","soundcloud":"https://soundcloud.com/soulection/soulection-radio-show-547"},"state":"published","title":"Soulection Radio Show #547","artwork":"images/episodes/soulection-radio-show-547.jpg","content":"A fusion of dub, R&B edits, nostalgic tunes, and new music.\n<!--more-->\n","profile":"QiEFFErt688","duration":7200,"location":"US","published_at":"2022-04-30T00:00:00+00:00"},"title":"Joe Kay's Session","position":0}},{"id":"bS8pE7ALLkQ","position":41,"timestamp":"01:35:28","rawTrack":"Jimmy Edgar - HYDRANT","track":{"id":"YZdtHW_DNWM","path":"/artists/jimmy-edgar/tracks/hydrant/","slug":"hydrant","title":"Hydrant","artist":{"slug":"jimmy-edgar","title":"Jimmy Edgar"},"artwork":"images/artists/jimmy-edgar/tracks/hydrant.jpg"},"chapter":{"show":{"id":"9MtqvaStm34","slug":"547","tags":[6,3,6,15],"links":{"appleMusic":"https://music.apple.com/gb/station/episode-547/ra.1619426080","soundcloud":"https://soundcloud.com/soulection/soulection-radio-show-547"},"state":"published","title":"Soulection Radio Show #547","artwork":"images/episodes/soulection-radio-show-547.jpg","content":"A fusion of dub, R&B edits, nostalgic tunes, and new music.\n<!--more-->\n","profile":"QiEFFErt688","duration":7200,"location":"US","published_at":"2022-04-30T00:00:00+00:00"},"title":"Joe Kay's Session","position":0}},{"id":"n6yIUEEbLdU","position":12,"timestamp":null,"rawTrack":"Jimmy Edgar - LBLB Detroit","track":{"id":"oVjFBSFtfBk","path":"/artists/jimmy-edgar/tracks/lblb-detroit/","slug":"lblb-detroit","title":"LBLB Detroit","artist":{"slug":"jimmy-edgar","title":"Jimmy Edgar"},"artwork":"images/artists/jimmy-edgar/tracks/lblb-detroit.jpg"},"chapter":{"show":{"id":"xEj4AlSU7Es","slug":"137","tags":[1,3,15],"links":{"soundcloud":"https://soundcloud.com/soulection/soulection-radio-show-137-w-mr"},"state":"published","title":"Soulection Radio Show #137 w/ Mr. Carmack & Mikos Da Gawd","artwork":"/images/episodes/137.jpg","content":"\nMikos Da Gawd and Mr. Carmack each drop amazing sets of unreleased, original productions.\n\n<!--more-->\n\nJoe Kay kicked things off for the first half of the show! He dropped a lot of exclusives and forgotten gems. Mikos Da Gawd dropped a 30+ minute DJ set that consisted of many gems and original productions from the man himself. Mr. Carmack wrapped up the show with an amazing listening session of all of his latest unreleased works. Man, all we gotta say is that Carmack is one of the best in the game right now. \n\n\nThanks to [true listener^^](https://soundcloud.com/true_listener) for supplying this tracklist.\n","profile":"QiEFFErt688","duration":10806,"location":"US","published_at":"2013-07-20T00:00:00+00:00"},"title":"Joe Kay's Set","position":0}},{"id":"WF2Dcw2Sp0E","position":23,"timestamp":null,"rawTrack":"Jimmy Edgar - Sleep Connexion","track":{"id":"YymD5zLOo8M","path":"/artists/jimmy-edgar/tracks/sleep-connexion/","slug":"sleep-connexion","title":"Sleep Connexion","artist":{"slug":"jimmy-edgar","title":"Jimmy Edgar"},"artwork":"images/artists/jimmy-edgar/tracks/sleep-connexion.jpg"},"chapter":{"show":{"id":"7vHj7jlvMRk","slug":"156","tags":[1,3,15],"links":{"soundcloud":"https://soundcloud.com/soulection/soulection-radio-show-156-w-j"},"state":"published","title":"Soulection Radio Show #156 w/ J-Louis","artwork":"/images/episodes/156.jpg","content":"Joe Kay is joined by Soulection's very own iPhone producer J-Louis.\n\n<!--more-->\nAs some of you may or may not know, J-Louis produces all his music on the iPhone [(Nano Studio App)](https://apps.apple.com/gb/developer/blip-interactive-ltd/id382263654?at=1010lMz4). He even put out a free EP with us in the beginning of the year entitled [\"Balanced\"](https://soulection.bandcamp.com/album/balanced-ep) which was also produced entirely on the iPhone. This 20 year-old from Azusa, CA is really a special guy who we feel is going to be BIG in the near future as long as he stays on track with his progression.\n\nJ-Louis played an exclusive set for a little over 30 minutes with all his recent unreleased productions and then chopped it up with us about his musical background (Drummer since he was 8 years-old & played in a Hardcore band & toured when he was 12) and how he purchased a stolen Macbook Pro (without knowing) to start producing on a computer that was eventually stolen -- forcing him to produce on his iPhone again. \n\nWhat a journey! Joe Kay also made sure to talk about his experience at the Yeezus tour this past Friday and later went into a heavy discussion about rumors of Soulection being part of Free-masonry/Illuminati. Very interesting and informative conversations going on as always.\n\n\nThanks to [true listener^^](https://soundcloud.com/true_listener) for supplying this tracklist.","profile":"QiEFFErt688","duration":10844,"location":"US","published_at":"2013-12-14T00:00:00+00:00"},"title":"Joe Kay's Set","position":0}},{"id":"xycu8w8fixI","position":62,"timestamp":null,"rawTrack":"Jimmy Edgar - LBLB Detroit","track":{"id":"oVjFBSFtfBk","path":"/artists/jimmy-edgar/tracks/lblb-detroit/","slug":"lblb-detroit","title":"LBLB Detroit","artist":{"slug":"jimmy-edgar","title":"J